  "worked_solution": "Let $x$ be the measure of the angle $∠C,$ then $m∠A=2x$ and $m∠B=2x+x=3x.$\n\nSince the sum of the interior angles is ${180}^{∘}$, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠B+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2x+3x+x & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 6x & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & =2\\cdot {30}^{∘}={60}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠B & =3\\cdot {30}^{∘}={90}^{∘}, \\\\ m∠C & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $△ABC$ is a right triangle because it has a right angle ($m∠B={90}^{∘}$).",
